petrus-observation-http
Copyright 2026 Seasoned

This package is a Haskell port of the observation HTTP adapter of Petrus
(petrus.engine.observation_http, by Henrique Bastos), pinned under
upstream/petrus and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It
follows the adapter's behavior and the HTTP profile of
spec/observation-protocol-v1.md, and its test suite ports the upstream tests
in tests/petrus/engine/test_observation_http.py. The package itself is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

The test and benchmark scripts in test/ and bench/ run the upstream Petrus
code from its pinned virtual environment to record the reference behavior;
no upstream source is included in the library.

Through petrus-http-core, the server reproduces the observable behavior of
CPython's http.server and urllib.parse (the Python Software Foundation
License); no CPython source code is included.
